; Checkpoint flags: which checkpoint is the active respawn point
;
; Nine bytes, one for each checkpoint that can be reached (checkpoint 0 is the trigger in the Abandoned church, room
; 7; checkpoints 1-8 are the ringed crosses of type 3 in rooms 8, 11, 12, 14, 15, 19, 21 and 23). At most one is
; nonzero: touching a checkpoint (#R$A688) first clears all nine, then sets its own byte to 2 (and plays sound 9); the
; church trigger (#R$A615) sets byte 0 to 1. The sprite frame of a checkpoint is bit 1 of its byte (ringed cross lit
; up once active). #R$BDF3 scans the bytes for the first nonzero one: its index selects the respawn record in the
; table #R$BE2A (room, row, column); if all nine are zero the tenth record is used, the start of the game in room 5.
; Zeroed at the start of a game.
@label=CheckpointFlag0
g$8543 DEFB $00 ; room 7 (church trigger)
@label=CheckpointFlag1
 $8544 DEFB $00 ; room 8
@label=CheckpointFlag2
 $8545 DEFB $00 ; room 11
@label=CheckpointFlag3
 $8546 DEFB $00 ; room 12
@label=CheckpointFlag4
 $8547 DEFB $00 ; room 14
@label=CheckpointFlag5
 $8548 DEFB $00 ; room 15
@label=CheckpointFlag6
 $8549 DEFB $00 ; room 19
@label=CheckpointFlag7
 $854A DEFB $00 ; room 21
@label=CheckpointFlag8
 $854B DEFB $00 ; room 23
